     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. It is 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Doses above the maximum raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and they give no added glycemic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose you have in mind\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
